Natl Acad Sci USA</source><volume>102</volume><fpage>2980</fpage><lpage>2985</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15710888</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001732-Reed1"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Reed</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name><name><surname>Caruana</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><name><surname>Batchelor</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></name><name><surname>Thompson</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name><name><surname>Crabb</surname><given-names>BS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Targeted disruption of an erythrocyte binding antigen in Plasmodium falciparum is associated with a switch toward a sialic acid-independent pathway of invasion.</article-title><source>Proc Natl Acad Sci U S A</source><volume>97</volume><fpage>7509</fpage><lpage>7514</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10861015</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001732-Hodder1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hodder</surname><given-names>AN</given-names></name><name><surname>Crewther</surname><given-names>PE</given-names></name><name><surname>Anders</surname><given-names>RF</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Specificity of the protective antibody response to apical membrane antigen 1.</article-title><source>Infect Immun</source><volume>69</volume><fpage>3286</fpage><lpage>3294</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11292751</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001732-Cohen1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cohen</surname><given-names>GH</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilcox</surname><given-names>WC</given-names></name><name><surname>Sodora</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name><name><surname>Long</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Levin</surname><given-names>JZ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1988</year><article-title>Expression of herpes simplex virus type 1 glycoprotein D deletion mutants in mammalian cells.</article-title><source>J Virol</source><volume>62</volume><fpage>1932</fpage><lpage>1940</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2452897</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001732-Chitnis1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chitnis</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></name><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>LH</given-names></name></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>Identification of the erythrocyte binding domains of <italic>Plasmodium vivax</italic> and <italic>Plasmodium knowlesi</italic> proteins involved in erythrocyte invasion.</article-title><source>J Exp Med</source><volume>180</volume><fpage>497</fpage><lpage>506</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8046329</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001732-Treeck1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Treeck</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Struck</surname><given-names>NS</given-names></name><name><surname>Haase</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Langer</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Herrmann</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>A Conserved Region in the EBL proteins is implicated in microneme targeting of the malaria parasite <italic>Plasmodium falciparum</italic>.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>281</volume><fpage>31995</fpage><lpage>32003</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16935855</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001732-Ghoneim1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ghoneim</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><n